{
  "_comment": [
    "Packet id mappings, keyed by state and direction.",
    "",
    "Each entry is a list of {from, id} ranges. 'from' is the protocol version at",
    "which that id takes effect; it stays in effect until the next range starts.",
    "Only packets HyperGravel actually decodes appear here \u2014 everything absent is",
    "forwarded as an opaque slice, which is most of PLAY.",
    "",
    "HANDSHAKE, STATUS, LOGIN and CONFIGURATION ids have been stable across the",
    "supported range and are reliable.",
    "",
    "PLAY ids shift nearly every release and MUST be verified against a generated",
    "protocol dump before production \u2014 see docs/PROTOCOL.md. A wrong id here does",
    "not corrupt the stream (the decoder falls back to raw forwarding on any decode",
    "failure) but it does silently disable the corresponding interception, so",
    "verify rather than assume.",
    "",
    "Protocol versions: 764=1.20.2 765=1.20.3 766=1.20.5 767=1.21 768=1.21.2",
    "769=1.21.4 770=1.21.5 771=1.21.6 772=1.21.7 773=1.21.9 774=1.21.11 776=26.2",
    "",
    "'encodeOnly' marks a packet the proxy writes but never wants to read. It is",
    "left out of the id lookup table, so a backend sending one stays on the raw",
    "passthrough path instead of being decoded and re-encoded for nothing.",
    "",
    "Ids at 776 were checked against ViaVersion's own packet tables, which are the",
    "same tables the translation layer uses."
  ],
